==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|m|u}}

===Etymology===
From Common Germanic *''[[murthaz]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*Hyphenation: mur·ha
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:Finnish:-urhɑ|-urhɑ]]
*{{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈmurhɑ]}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun|murh|type=koira}}

# [[murder|Murder]].
# {{law|lang=fi}} [[murder|Murder]], [[homicide]] (''premeditated and/or more brutal, and, therefore, more aggravated than [[tappo]]'').

====Usage notes====
*(''law:'') The order of homicidal crimes in Finnish legislation &mdash;by how severe they are considered in Finnish law&mdash; is the following with the least aggravated being first and the most aggravated being the fourth:
::1. [[kuolemantuottamus]] ("involuntary manslaughter")
:::-> 2. [[surma]] ("voluntary manslaughter under mitigating circumstances")
::::-> 3. [[tappo]] ("voluntary manslaughter" or "homicide", under no mitigating circumstances)
:::::-> 4. [[murha]] ("murder", "homicide", killing of a person by another under aggravating circumstances, premeditated and/or brutal).

